<programme start="20261029100000 +0000" stop="20261029110000 +0000" channel="Smithsonian Channel"><title lang="en">Combat Ships</title><sub-title lang="en">Torpedo Boats</sub-title><desc lang="en">From tests in the River Thames, to the German&apos;s deadly U-boat attacks in World War II, this episode explores the silent threat of submarines.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><category lang="en">History</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-PG</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p13658854_b_s4_aj.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261029110000 +0000" stop="20261029120000 +0000" channel="Smithsonian Channel"><title lang="en">Combat Ships</title><sub-title lang="en">Secrets of the Sea</sub-title><desc lang="en">Stories of espionage at sea, including deadly U-boat cat-and-mouse games during WWI, the sinking of the Lusitania, a gun-smuggling private yacht that made history, and liners turned troopships.</desc><credits><actor>Ben Major</actor></credits><category lang="en">Documentary</category><category lang="en">History</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-PG</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p13658854_b_v12_ai.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261029120000 +0000" stop="20261029130000 +0000" channel="Smithsonian Channel"><title lang="en">Combat Ships</title><sub-title lang="en">The Battle of Trafalgar</sub-title><desc lang="en">The legendary Battle of Trafalgar in 1805, which pitted Napoleon&apos;s French ships against a British armada under the command of Admiral Horatio Nelson.</desc><credits><actor>Ben Major</actor></credits><category lang="en">Documentary</category><category lang="en">History</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-PG</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p13658854_b_v12_ai.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261029130000 +0000" stop="20261029140000 +0000" channel="Smithsonian Channel"><title lang="en">Combat Ships</title><sub-title lang="en">Secrets and Lies</sub-title><desc lang="en">A look at how the art of deception was used by naval forces in the first half of the 20th century; in 1939, the German raider Atlantis was equipped with fake funnels, while its sailors dressed as women pushing strollers to fool Allied merchant ships.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><category lang="en">History</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-PG</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p13658854_b_v12_ai.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261029140000 +0000" stop="20261029150000 +0000" channel="Smithsonian Channel"><title lang="en">Combat Ships</title><sub-title lang="en">Galleons and Privateers</sub-title><desc lang="en">Revolutionary ship design helped Sir John Hawkins and Sir Francis Drake lead England to defeat the Spanish Armada and become a world power.</desc><credits><actor>Ben Major</actor></credits><category lang="en">Documentary</category><category lang="en">History</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-PG</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p13658854_b_v12_ai.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261029150000 +0000" stop="20261029160000 +0000" channel="Smithsonian Channel"><title lang="en">Combat Ships</title><sub-title lang="en">The Fast and Furious</sub-title><desc lang="en">A look at Naval warfare&apos;s fastest combat ships and how the advantage of speed determined the outcome of some of the great seas battles of the last 150 years.</desc><credits><actor>Ben Major</actor></credits><category lang="en">Documentary</category><category lang="en">History</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-PG</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p13658854_b_v12_ai.jpg"/></programme>
